   MMaarrggiinnss
       A few terminals expose a means of changing their left  and  right  mar‐
       gins.  ttaabbss supports this feature with an option.

       ++mm _m_a_r_g_i_n
            The effect depends on whether the terminal has the margin capabil‐
            ities:

            •   If the terminal provides the capability for setting  the  left
                margin,  ttaabbss  uses  this,  and adjusts the available tab stop
                widths.

            •   If the terminal does not provide the margin capabilities, ttaabbss
                imitates their effect, putting tab stops at appropriate places
                on each line.  The terminal's left margin is not modified.

            If the _m_a_r_g_i_n parameter is omitted, the default is 10.  Use ++mm00 to
            reset  the  left  margin, that is, to make it the left edge of the
            terminal's display.  Before setting a left margin, ttaabbss resets the
            margin  to reduce problems that might arise from moving the cursor
            to the left of the current left margin.

       When setting or resetting the left margin,  ttaabbss  may  also  reset  the
       right margin.

